      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The first nucleophilic perfluoroalkylation of arenes is based on the arene π-system activation via (η6-arene)tricarbonylchromium complexes. Perfluoroalkyl anions generated from Me3SiRF and a fluoride ion source [Me4N]F exclusively attack the arene ligand under mild conditions. The formed negatively charged analogs of Meisenheimer adducts readily undergo a one-pot oxidation to perfluoroalkyl arenes."},
